cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software or evaluation protocol, please cite it as below."
title: "InventOR: A Human-Reviewed, Prompt-Configured Large Language Model Decision Support System for Material-Level Inventory Control"
authors:
  - family-names: Dressino
    given-names: Aris
    affiliation: "TUM School of Management, Technical University of Munich"
version: 1.2.0
date-released: "2026-10-06"
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/DressPD/inventor_public"
abstract: >-
  A confidentiality-screened public release of InventOR: analysis code, the
  anonymized variable schema, aggregate evaluation results for Run 1, Run 2,
  and Run 3, manuscript sources, and an integrity manifest for a
  prompt-configured large-language-model workflow that generates
  material-level (r,Q) inventory policies without project-specific model
  training or fine-tuning.
keywords:
  - large language models
  - inventory management
  - operations research
  - reproducibility
  - prompt engineering
  - material-level inventory control
